borrow-temporary-outside-a-call.slp:2:16: error[SL0200]: only a binding can be borrowed here
  |
 2 |   (let text (& "a literal has no name to borrow"))
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: give the value a name with `let`, or borrow it where a call takes it
  = note: a borrowed temporary dies when the call it was passed to returns, so there is nowhere to release one that is not an argument
